# text = Crimsworth , elegantly dressed in satin and lace , blooming in youth and health , vouchsafed me no more notice than was expressed by a distant move ; Crimsworth , of course , never spoke to me ; I was introduced to none of the band of young ladies , who , enveloped in silvery clouds of white gauze and muslin , sat in array against me on the opposite side of a long and large room ; in fact , I was fairly isolated , and could but contemplate the shining ones from affar , and when weary of such a dazzling scene , turn for a change to the consideration of the carpet pattern .
