# text = I have mentioned his dark locks -- they were brushed sideways above a white and sufficiently expansive forehead ; his cheek had a rather hectic freshness ; his features might have done well on canvas , but indifferently in marble : they were plastic ; character had set a stamp upon each ; expression re-cast them at her pleasure , and strange metamorphoses she wrought , giving him now the mien of a morose bull , and anon that of an arch and mischievous girl ; more frequently , the two semblances were blent , and a queer , composite countenance they made .
