# text = I shut the door and sat down at the desk ; my hands , recently washed in half-frozen water , were still numb ; I could not write till they had regained vitality , so I went on thinking , and still the theme of my thoughts was the Self-dissatisfaction troubled exceedingly the current of my meditations said my conscience , or whatever it is that within ourselves takes ourselves to task said I sullenly reiterated the inward voice I growled ; but nevertheless I drew out a packet of letters and commenced my task -- task thankless and bitter as that of the Israelite crawling over the sun-baked fields of Egypt in search of straw and stubble wherewith to accomplish his tale of bricks .
