# text = On the first landing I met a Flemish housemaid : she had wooden shoes , a short red petticoat , a printed cotton bedgown , her face was broad , her physiognomy eminently stupid ; when I spoke to her in French , she answered me in Flemish , with an air the reverse of civil ; yet I thought her charming ; if she was not pretty or polite , she was , I conceived , very picturesque ; she reminded me of the female figures in certain Dutch paintings I had seen in other years at Seacombe Hall .
