# text = A fourth maitresse I sometimes saw who seemed to come daily to teach needlework , or netting , or lace-mending , or some such flimsy art ; but of her I never had more than a passing glimpse , as she sat in the CARRE , with her frames and some dozen of the elder pupils about her , consequently I had no opportunity of studying her character , or even of observing her person much ; the latter , I remarked , had a very English air for a maitresse , otherwise it was not striking ; of character I should think ; she possessed but little , as her pupils seemed constantly " en revolte " against her authority .
