# text = It was the question I placed before my mind as I stirred my cup of coffee with a half-pistolet ( we never had spoons ), Pelet meantime being seated opposite , his pallid face looking as knowing and more haggard than usual , his blue eye turned , now sternly on his boys and ushers , and now graciously on me said I ; and meeting Pelet's false glance and insinuating smile , I thanked heaven that I had last night opened my window and read by the light of a full moon the true meaning of that guileful countenance .
