# text = At times I wondered what she meant by giving herself such trouble to win me , when the more profitable Pelet was already in her nets , and when , too , she was aware that I possessed her secret , for I had not scrupled to tell her as much : but the fact is that as it was her nature to doubt the reality and under-value the worth of modesty , affection , disinterestedness -- to regard these qualities as foibles of character -- so it was equally her tendency to consider pride , hardness , selfishness , as proofs of strength .
