# text = Human beings -- human children especially -- seldom deny themselves the pleasure of exercising a power which they are conscious of possessing , even though that power consist only in a capacity to make others wretched ; a pupil whose sensations are duller than those of his instructor , while his nerves are tougher and his bodily strength perhaps greater , has an immense advantage over that instructor , and he will generally use it relentlessly , because the very young , very healthy , very thoughtless , know neither how to sympathize nor how to spare .
