# text = I hate boldness -- that boldness which is of the brassy brow and insensate nerves ; but I love the courage of the strong heart , the fervour of the generous blood ; I loved with passion the light of Frances Evans' clear hazel eye when it did not fear to look straight into mine ; I loved the tones with which she uttered the words I loved the movement with which she confided her hand to my hand ; I loved her as she stood there , penniless and parentless ; for a sensualist charmless , for me a treasure -- my best object of sympathy on earth , thinking such thoughts as I thought , feeling such feelings as I felt ; my ideal of the shrine in which to seal my stores of love ; personification of discretion and forethought , of diligence and perseverance , of self-denial and self-control -- those guardians , those trusty keepers of the gift I longed to confer on her -- the gift of all my affections ; model of truth and honour , of independence and conscientiousness -- those refiners and sustainers of an honest life ; silent possessor of a well of tenderness , of a flame , as genial as still , as pure as quenchless , of natural feeling , natural passion -- those sources of refreshment and comfort to the sanctuary of home .
