# text = For a long time Pelet bore with my frigid demeanour very patiently ; he even increased his attentions ; but finding that even a cringing politeness failed to thaw or move me , he at last altered too ; in his turn he cooled ; his invitations ceased ; his countenance became suspicious and overcast , and I read in the perplexed yet brooding aspect of his brow , a constant examination and comparison of premises , and an anxious endeavour to draw thence some explanatory inference .
