# text = At that time , I was not : I used to rise each morning eager to shake off his yoke , and go out with my portmanteau under my arm , if a beggar , at least a freeman ; and in the evening , when I came back from the pensionnat de demoiselles , a certain pleasant voice in my ear ; a certain face , so intelligent , yet so docile , so reflective , yet so soft , in my eyes ; a certain cast of character , at once proud and pliant , sensitive and sagacious , serious and ardent , in my head ; a certain tone of feeling , fervid and modest , refined and practical , pure and powerful , delighting and troubling my memory -- visions of new ties I longed to contract , of new duties I longed to undertake , had taken the rover and the rebel out of me , and had shown endurance of my hated lot in the light of a Spartan virtue .
