# text = He could not be aware that since then youth and loveliness had been to me everyday objects ; that I had studied them at leisure and closely , and had seen the plain texture of truth under the embroidery of appearance ; nor could he , keen-sighted as he was , penetrate into my heart , search my brain , and read my peculiar sympathies and antipathies ; he had not known me long enough , or well enough , to perceive how low my feelings would ebb under some influences , powerful over most minds ; how high , how fast they would flow under other influences , that perhaps acted with the more intense force on me , because they acted on me alone .
