# text = Accounts being wound up , and our professional connection disposed of , we both agreed that , as mammon was not our master , nor his service that in which we desired to spend our lives ; as our desires were temperate , and our habits unostentatious , we had now abundance to live on -- abundance to leave our boy ; and should besides always have a balance on hand , which , properly managed by right sympathy and unselfish activity , might help philanthropy in her enterprises , and put solace into the hand of charity .
